.\" A synthetic mdoc(7) page, the counterpart of greet.1 for the BSD macros.
.Dd August 23, 2026
.Dt MGREET 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mgreet ,
.Nm mhello
.Nd greet somebody by name
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl v
.Op Fl n Ar times
.Ar name ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility writes a greeting for each
.Ar name
to standard output.
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl v
Write the greeting to
.Pa /dev/tty
as well, and report the version.
.It Fl n Ar times
Repeat each greeting
.Ar times
times.
.El
.Pp
An
.Sm off
.Oo user @ Oc host
.Sm on
operand greets a remote machine, on
.Ux
systems only.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Greet two people twice:
.Bd -literal
mgreet -n 2 ada grace
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr greet 1 ,
.Xr write 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Fn greet name
interface conforms to
.St -p1003.1-2008 .
